    // Apply path filter
    if let Some(pname) = path_filter {
        candidates.retain(|s| s.cheatpath_name == pname);
        // If no candidates but path_filter specified and file not found, we will create at that cheatpath even if readonly? Wait original: `cheat -p readonly -e ro3` gave error "failed to get writeable path: no writeable cheatpaths found" because readonly path has no writable. That indicates when creating new sheet with -p readonly (which is readonly), it should error because no writable. So we need to handle.
    } else {
        // If tag filter specified? Original edit with tag filter? Not tested, but tag filter for edit maybe not used. We'll ignore tag for edit? But spec says cheat -p work -e foo/bar uses path. We'll also support tag filter for view but edit may also support -t? Let's check original help: edit option says "Open _CHEATSHEET_ for editing." but flags -p and -t can be combined? In earlier test, edit with -t not yet tested. We'll implement path filter only for edit.

